# 2D Fluid Simulation
A two-dimensional incompressible fluid simulator written in C, with a Python viewer for real-time visualization. The project simulates flow through a wind tunnel. It can display smoke transport, vorticity magnitude, and velocity magnitude around several obstacle geometries. I was inspired by a [Sebastian Lague's Youtube video](https://youtu.be/Q78wvrQ9xsU?si=5V0-nEyfrvVwteIh).

<p align="center">
  <img src="assets/cylinder-vorticity.png" alt="Vorticity field and vortex shedding behind a circular cylinder" width="900">
</p>

<p align="center"><em>Vorticity field and vortex shedding behind a circular cylinder.</em></p>

## Features
- No-slip obstacle boundaries
- Stationary or moving upper and lower tunnel walls
- Open right-hand outlet and prescribed left-hand inflow
- Pulsed smoke bands or continuous horizontal tracer streams
- Three visualization modes:
  - Smoke concentration
  - Vorticity magnitude
  - Velocity magnitude
- Multiple built-in geometries

## Project Structure
```text
fluid.c    C simulation and binary frame generator
view.py    Python real-time visualizer
Makefile   Build and run commands
```

## Dependencies
- NumPy
- Matplotlib

## Build
Using the Makefile:
```bash
make
```
On some Windows installations, use:
```bash
mingw32-make
```
Alternatively, compile manually:
```bash
gcc -O3 -std=c11 -Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic fluid.c -o fluid.exe -lm
```

## Run
Run the viewer directly:
```bash
python view.py --scene cylinder --frames 2400
```
Or build and run through the Makefile:
```bash
make run SCENE=cylinder FRAMES=2400
```
Replace `make` with `mingw32-make` if required by your Windows toolchain.

## Available Scenes
| Scene argument | Geometry |
| --- | --- |
| `none` | Empty wind tunnel |
| `cylinder` | Single circular cylinder |
| `rectangle` | Rectangular obstacle |
| `ellipse` | Elliptical obstacle |
| `nozzle` | Converging nozzle followed by a cylinder |
| `airfoil` | Symmetric NACA-style airfoil at a configurable angle |
| `venturi` | Smooth converging-diverging passage |
| `cylinder-array` | Staggered array of circular cylinders |

